        "original_id": "0c4b7701-f793-5250-b142-d88b5a92b913",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Places: Gibraltar, Europa Point, southern Spain\n- Organizations: British Overseas Territories\n- People: Ibrahim al-Ibrahim, King Fahd bin Abdulaziz al-Saud, Elizabeth II\n- Buildings: Ibrahim-al-Ibrahim Mosque\n- Concepts: British monarch, head of state\n\nFacts:\n- The Ibrahim-al-Ibrahim Mosque is also known as the King Fahd bin Abdulaziz al-Saud Mosque and the Mosque of the Custodian of the Two Holy Mosques.\n- The Ibrahim-al-Ibrahim Mosque is located at Europa Point in Gibraltar.\n- Gibraltar is a British overseas territory on a peninsula connected to southern Spain.\n- The British Overseas Territories share the British monarch as head of state.\n- Elizabeth II is the British monarch shared as head of state by the British Overseas Territories.",
